==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kæ.təˈtɑn.ɪk/|lang=en}}
*: {{rhymes|ɒnɪk|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} Of, relating to, or suffering from [[catatonia]]; (''loosely'') motionless and unresponsive, as from [[shock]]; [[withdrawn]].
#* '''1967''', unnamed doctor in 1967, [[w:Frederick Wiseman|Frederick Wiseman]] (director), ''[[w:Titicut Follies|Titicut Follies]]'' (documentary film), quoted in '''2004''', Jerrold R. Brandell (editor), ''Celluloid Couches, Cinematic Clients'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=F4O3u463ECkC&pg=PA118&dq=%22more%7Cmost+catatonic%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ndE2U-_xHMebkgWAxYC4Cw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20catatonic%22&f=false page 118],
#*: However, he was looking a lot more '''catatonic''' and depressed before and sometimes we find that on the anti-depressants you remove the depression and uncover the paranoid stuff and we may have to give him larger quantities of tranquilizers just to tone this down.
#* {{quote-text|year=2004|author=William Meninger|title=1012 Monastery Road: A Spiritual Journey|page=19|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=vm4ws5wirGMC&pg=PA19&dq=%22more%7Cmost+catatonic%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ndE2U-_xHMebkgWAxYC4Cw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20catatonic%22&f=false|passage=Further and further he would withdraw from the world, becoming more and more '''catatonic''' — withdrawing completely from his hateful world to the only real and secure comfort he had ever known, the womb.}}
#* {{quote-text|year=2006|author=David H. Brendel|title=Healing Psychiatry|page=119|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=tkqZnX6OCiMC&pg=PA119&dq=%22more%7Cmost+catatonic%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ndE2U-_xHMebkgWAxYC4Cw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20catatonic%22&f=false|passage=It was plausible that Cara became more '''catatonic''' in order to avoid a painful and overwhelming confrontation with terrifying but repressed memories of child abuse.}}
#* {{quote-text|year=2009|author=Nicole Chénier-Cullen|title=I Found My Thrill on Parliament Hill|page=37|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=9buAFrLl6VIC&pg=PA37&dq=%22more%7Cmost+catatonic%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ndE2U-_xHMebkgWAxYC4Cw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20catatonic%22&f=false|passage=The fact that he was not twirling his kiss curl underscored his '''catatonic''' state of mind. I didn't know who was more '''catatonic'''—Brentwood, the minister, or myself.}}
#* {{quote-text|year=2011|author=T. F. Bohn|title=Dirty Jerry: Faith In the Real World|page=64|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=Fc-9QIusWxIC&pg=PA64&dq=%22more%7Cmost+catatonic%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ndE2U-_xHMebkgWAxYC4Cw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22more%7Cmost%20catatonic%22&f=false|passage=A very young Ensign, in his first real contact with combat conditions, was in charge but was almost of no use as he began to hyper-ventilate and became more and more '''catatonic''' the closer they got to shore.}}

